  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (sentiment ≤ 0.00) to counteract overconfidence.",
    "Reduce forecast bias by applying a 10-15% downward correction if model consistently overestimates prices in recent 7-14 day windows.",
    "Apply lag correction: if true outcome is higher than forecasted 3-5 days prior, reduce current forecast by 5-10% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "Cap upward forecasts after sharp spikes (e.g., >15% above recent mean) to prevent overshoot and volatility overcorrection.",
    "Use mean reversion heuristic: if 30-day moving average of true outcomes is > 5% above forecast, reduce forecast by 2-3% per day until convergence.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to sentiment: if sentiment > 0.25, adjust forecast upward by 2-5% to reflect bullish momentum; if sentiment < -0.25, adjust downward by 2-5% to reflect bearish sentiment."
  ]
}
